The PR description says "all new helpers are exported for direct testing", and both wrappers are exercised transitively through `asArray` (wrapper unwrap + `result` recursion suites both pass, 100% statement coverage). But the exported symbols themselves are never referenced from the test file, so a future rename of `asArrayRuns`/`asArrayResult` would not break any test even if `asArray` stopped calling them.

A two-line addition to the existing `asArray (gh-1193)` suite closes that gap:

```js
test('wrapper helpers are directly testable', function() {
    var reporter = loadReporter();
    assert.deepEqual(reporter.asArrayRuns({ jobs: [1] }), [1]);
    assert.equal(reporter.asArrayRuns({}), null);
    assert.deepEqual(reporter.asArrayResult({ result: '[2]' }), [2]);
    assert.equal(reporter.asArrayResult({}), null);
});
```

Optional polish — the behaviour itself is fully covered via `asArray`.

